  "details": "My avatar has glasses and I've noticed since the last update that the glass shader I was using appears to be broken. Depending on what angle my avatar looks in a mirror the shader will either work properly or disappear entirely. You'll notice in my screenshots if I lean backwards the shader disappears, but if I lean forward it works normally.\nI've tried two different glass shaders on my avatar and the problem was identical regardless of what shader I was using, which makes me think it's a problem with the way VRchat is rendering them and not a problem with my avatar.\n\nFor reference I've tried MKglass free and Rollthered Fake HDR refraced glass shader.",
